<title>FRANCE: Thomson-CSF wins two simulator contracts.</title>
<headline>Thomson-CSF wins two simulator contracts.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thomson-CSF said the French defence procurement agency had awarded it a contract to upgrade the Mirage 2000N simulator which enetered service in 1988 at the Luxeuil air base.</p>
<p>It also awarded it a contract to link the French army's Leclerc tank crew simulators using Distributed Interactive Simulation (DIS) -- which allows several crew to simulate that they are together in the same battle situation.</p>
<p>Thomson-CSF gave no financial details.</p>
</text>
